WEBVTT

00:01.410 --> 00:03.380
Previously on "Final Space"...

00:03.410 --> 00:05.030
Nightfall reveals
that she's Quinn?

00:05.070 --> 00:06.310
From the future?!

00:06.350 --> 00:07.660
Whoa! Hot diggity!

00:07.690 --> 00:09.690
Also, she has a thing for Gary,

00:09.730 --> 00:11.830
but there's no time
for cosmic three-ways...

00:11.870 --> 00:15.730
because our crew has a breach
to close in space...

00:15.770 --> 00:17.050
and fast.

00:17.080 --> 00:19.360
♪♪

00:20.050 --> 00:24.160
H.U.E.: Gary, you have
two minutes of oxygen left.

00:24.190 --> 00:27.190
[ Breathing heavily ]

00:27.230 --> 00:29.020
Can we...

00:29.060 --> 00:31.510
change that
to something more cheerful?

00:31.540 --> 00:33.270
Sure, Gary.

00:33.300 --> 00:34.580
Cookies.

00:34.620 --> 00:37.170
Act like you're baking
a big batch of cookies.

00:37.200 --> 00:40.790
Gary, the cookies will be done
in two minutes.

00:40.830 --> 00:43.900
Oh...fantastic.

00:43.940 --> 00:45.870
I love cookies.

00:45.900 --> 00:48.460
What kind of cookies
we talkin' about?

00:48.490 --> 00:50.530
Butter wheat crunch.

00:50.560 --> 00:53.460
That's...not a cookie.

00:53.500 --> 00:56.120
And you know that, H.U.E.

00:56.150 --> 00:57.950
You know that!

00:57.980 --> 01:07.130
♪♪

01:07.170 --> 01:16.380
♪♪

01:16.420 --> 01:25.840
♪♪

01:26.700 --> 01:28.290
♪♪

01:28.320 --> 01:29.840
Gary: Crew!

01:29.880 --> 01:33.160
Or legion of murdering
an irritatingly power-thirsty

01:33.190 --> 01:36.510
pint-sized imp
into a plethora of buttholes!

01:36.540 --> 01:38.580
Are you ready
to save the Earth?!

01:38.610 --> 01:40.920
-Hooray! Oh, yeah!
-Hooray! Hooray!

01:40.960 --> 01:43.340
The question is, Captain,
are youready?

01:43.370 --> 01:45.270
I'm so ready!

01:45.310 --> 01:46.580
I'm so not ready!

01:46.620 --> 01:48.660
How am I gonna save
an entire planet?

01:48.690 --> 01:50.110
I'm all for trying,

01:50.140 --> 01:53.830
but there's a high chance
we're all going to die!

01:53.870 --> 01:56.490
Yes. It's more or less
a done deal.

01:56.530 --> 01:58.530
That's not comforting
at all!

01:58.560 --> 02:00.940
I can do this, right?
Right?!

02:00.980 --> 02:02.980
Oh, this is impossible!

02:03.010 --> 02:05.600
Nothing is impossible

02:05.640 --> 02:08.020
if we apply our minds to it.

02:08.050 --> 02:11.440
H.U.E., do we know of a way
we can close this breach?

02:11.470 --> 02:13.340
No.Well, that's not good.

02:13.370 --> 02:14.610
Okay, uh, well...

02:14.650 --> 02:16.060
anything at all
we could do?

02:16.100 --> 02:18.620
Yes. You can kiss
your cheeks goodbye.

02:18.650 --> 02:20.000
You givin' me
a little clap back?

02:20.030 --> 02:22.170
You givin' me
the old clap back, H.U.E.?!

02:22.210 --> 02:23.550
I thought I'd give it a try

02:23.590 --> 02:25.800
before we implode
into nothingness.

02:25.830 --> 02:30.560
"Implode into nothingness,"
he said!

02:30.590 --> 02:33.390
Oh, my gosh.
Freaking Mondays.

02:33.420 --> 02:35.500
Gary,
am I gonna die?

02:35.530 --> 02:37.010
Are you trying
to cheer me up, KVN?

02:37.050 --> 02:40.290
Okay, because you dying would
be a wonderful development.

02:40.330 --> 02:42.470
♪ We're all gonna die

02:42.500 --> 02:43.680
♪ We're all gonna di--

02:43.710 --> 02:45.060
Shut the hell up, KVN.

02:45.090 --> 02:47.160
Or I will find ways.

02:47.200 --> 02:49.750
Actually, there is a way.

02:49.790 --> 02:53.690
H.U.E., set coordinates
for sector 12, region 6.79.

02:53.720 --> 02:57.310
Nightfall, that would fly us
directly into the sun

02:57.340 --> 02:58.860
at the heart
of the Orion Nebula.

02:58.900 --> 03:02.660
I know.We are not flying
into a sun!

03:02.690 --> 03:03.730
Do you want to live?

03:03.760 --> 03:05.250
Yes.
I would love to live.

03:05.280 --> 03:09.050
That's exactly freaking why
we're not flying into a sun!

03:09.080 --> 03:11.600
You're right.
We're going to lightfold in.

03:11.630 --> 03:14.570
That's freaking worse!

03:14.600 --> 03:16.430
You said it
like it was better,

03:16.470 --> 03:18.430
but that is
the opposite of better!

03:18.470 --> 03:19.780
I would never suggest this

03:19.820 --> 03:22.060
unless I knew something
you're not sharing.

03:22.090 --> 03:23.200
What do you know?

03:23.230 --> 03:27.060
Quinn, aren't you curious
how you became me?

03:27.100 --> 03:29.550
If that answers even
involves flying into a sun,

03:29.580 --> 03:30.760
I'm not curious.

03:30.790 --> 03:31.900
I don't think
anybody's curious.

03:31.930 --> 03:33.350
Aah!I'm curious!
Keep going!

03:33.380 --> 03:34.930
[ Cackles ]
-Must you, KVN?!

03:34.970 --> 03:37.040
Must you?!
Hee-hee hoo.

03:37.070 --> 03:38.040
Tell me.

03:38.070 --> 03:40.700
There's only one being
who can help us.

03:40.730 --> 03:42.110
A Titan
who inhabits a realm

03:42.150 --> 03:45.050
between our dimension and
the next called Inner Space.

03:45.080 --> 03:46.640
He came to me.

03:46.670 --> 03:49.120
At my lowest point.

03:49.150 --> 03:56.610
♪♪

03:56.650 --> 03:58.410
It's over.

03:58.440 --> 04:00.580
Everything is over.

04:00.610 --> 04:02.240
♪♪

04:02.270 --> 04:03.760
I'm coming, Gary.

04:03.790 --> 04:07.550
Bolo:
This is not your fate.

04:07.590 --> 04:11.760
I offer not madness,
but salvation.

04:13.110 --> 04:15.660
We can change
what has become.

04:15.700 --> 04:19.390
How?A machine to traverse time.

04:19.430 --> 04:21.080
You can construct it.

04:21.120 --> 04:23.120
With my help.

04:23.150 --> 04:25.570
Who are you?
Bolo.

04:25.610 --> 04:28.470
A fellow victim of infinity.

04:28.500 --> 04:31.850
And now we fight back.

04:31.890 --> 04:34.750
Little Cato: Who's Bolo?He's a Titan.

04:34.790 --> 04:37.000
The Titans are
terrible, vengeful creatures

04:37.030 --> 04:39.860
who poison the universe
with chaos.

04:39.900 --> 04:42.280
Each in charge
of a different realm.

04:42.310 --> 04:44.450
One broke ranks.

04:44.490 --> 04:46.320
Bolo.

04:46.350 --> 04:48.870
He saw there was a better way
and sealed off our dimension

04:48.900 --> 04:50.940
from the horrors of Final Space.

04:50.980 --> 04:53.870
They took revenge
and imprisoned him.

04:53.910 --> 04:56.190
He's the only one
who can help.

04:56.220 --> 04:57.840
[ Laughs ]
That's sick.

04:57.880 --> 05:00.050
Older hot Quinn
makes an excellent point.

05:00.090 --> 05:03.060
If Bolo's the only one
that can help us,

05:03.090 --> 05:04.370
we've got no choice.

05:04.400 --> 05:06.510
Chookity pok!Well said, Mooncake.

05:06.540 --> 05:08.510
Let's fly through a sun!

05:08.540 --> 05:09.790
Oh, my Lord,

05:09.820 --> 05:11.930
I cannot believe
we are doing this.

05:13.480 --> 05:15.070
♪♪

05:15.100 --> 05:17.800
Dimension phasing
is notoriously difficult.

05:17.830 --> 05:19.690
To see Bolo, we're going
to have to lightfold

05:19.730 --> 05:21.520
exactly through
the sun's aperture.

05:21.560 --> 05:25.800
If we are off by even one
degree, we burn up and die.

05:25.840 --> 05:28.460
Buckle up.
This will be a bumpy ride.

05:28.500 --> 05:31.080
All right, H.U.E.
Take us in!

05:31.120 --> 05:34.160
♪♪

05:34.190 --> 05:37.370
Entering into the corona
of the sun.

05:37.400 --> 05:42.480
♪♪

05:42.510 --> 05:45.750
The heat of the sun has melted
through the navigation system.

05:45.790 --> 05:48.930
You will need to manually
navigate it into the aperture.

05:48.960 --> 05:50.830
All right, I'll do it.

05:50.860 --> 05:52.280
But you're not a good pilot.

05:52.310 --> 05:55.280
Thank you very much for
believing in me, Quinn.

05:55.320 --> 05:56.730
Please do not screw this up.

05:56.770 --> 05:58.250
Okay, that's not helping!

05:58.280 --> 05:59.350
Concentrate, Gary.

05:59.390 --> 06:00.490
You gotta do this.

06:00.530 --> 06:01.940
Let's thread this needle.

06:01.980 --> 06:05.190
♪♪

06:05.220 --> 06:06.910
[ Grunting ]

06:06.950 --> 06:09.120
Come on, come on,
come on, come on!

06:09.160 --> 06:14.680
♪♪

06:14.710 --> 06:16.270
[ Screaming ]

06:16.300 --> 06:17.370
Gary! Center it!

06:17.410 --> 06:18.440
I got this!

06:18.480 --> 06:20.060
You got this,
Thunder Bandit!

06:20.100 --> 06:21.860
Quinn: No, you don't!
Center it!

06:21.890 --> 06:23.380
Oh, you're scaring me!
I'm scared!

06:23.410 --> 06:24.410
Center it!

06:24.450 --> 06:25.590
I'm very frightened!

06:25.620 --> 06:27.620
Gary!
Aah!

06:29.140 --> 06:31.700
Oh, my crap!

06:31.730 --> 06:33.150
Oh, my crap.

06:33.180 --> 06:34.700
♪♪

06:34.730 --> 06:38.220
Welcome to Inner Space.

06:38.250 --> 06:41.840
♪♪

06:43.980 --> 06:45.810
♪♪

06:45.850 --> 06:47.920
Just our luck.
He's asleep.

06:47.950 --> 06:50.650
Gary, he's been asleep
for 10,000 years.

06:50.680 --> 06:53.060
Well, then
why are we here?

06:53.100 --> 06:54.960
Wait for it.

06:55.000 --> 06:57.450
Wait for wha--

06:57.480 --> 07:01.170
[ All shouting ]

07:03.210 --> 07:08.080
[ Voices distorting ]

07:08.110 --> 07:11.180
[ Rumbling ]

07:11.220 --> 07:13.570
Get me the hell out of here!

07:13.600 --> 07:18.500
♪♪

07:18.540 --> 07:22.680
Did we just get sucked
into dude's mind?

07:22.710 --> 07:23.850
Don't worry,
that's normal.

07:23.890 --> 07:25.750
I am not okay with this --

07:25.790 --> 07:30.380
winter wonderland
of cosmic cotton candy!

07:30.410 --> 07:32.380
Aah! Aah!

07:32.410 --> 07:36.490
I'm just gonna put this down
right on this little lily pad.

07:36.520 --> 07:38.350
Oh, there we go.

07:38.380 --> 07:40.110
[ Sighs ]

07:40.140 --> 07:46.500
♪♪

07:46.530 --> 07:48.390
Oh, hey,
there's a guy.

07:48.430 --> 07:49.950
Hey. Hey!

07:49.980 --> 07:52.230
So, not sure we're
in the right place,

07:52.260 --> 07:53.850
but we got this thing --

07:53.880 --> 07:55.330
You're late!

07:55.370 --> 07:57.510
-Late?
-Yes, late!

07:57.540 --> 07:59.820
He's been waiting
on you for years!

07:59.850 --> 08:01.890
You're like
a giant flaming M&M.

08:01.920 --> 08:05.130
Excuse me?!
Are you giving me sass?!

08:05.170 --> 08:06.240
Hyah!
[ Grunts ]

08:06.270 --> 08:07.720
Oh! Freaking!
Did you just

08:07.760 --> 08:09.350
whack me in the face
with your stick?!

08:09.380 --> 08:11.070
Aah!

08:11.110 --> 08:13.760
You and I are not
gonna get along.

08:14.730 --> 08:18.010
[ All shouting ]

08:20.600 --> 08:21.980
Explain...

08:22.010 --> 08:23.570
to me...

08:23.600 --> 08:24.810
what just happened.

08:24.840 --> 08:27.020
We hopped over
to brain chamber two.

08:27.050 --> 08:28.160
Hopped?

08:28.190 --> 08:29.500
No, no, no, no!

08:29.540 --> 08:31.890
We were hurled --

08:35.920 --> 08:37.930
Oh, there's moisture.

08:37.960 --> 08:38.930
[ Gasps ]

08:38.960 --> 08:40.890
I think my eyes are bleeding!

08:40.930 --> 08:42.210
[ Laughing hysterically ]

08:42.240 --> 08:43.210
My eyes!

08:43.240 --> 08:45.110
Blood! Blood!

08:45.140 --> 08:48.700
[ Chuckles ] This is only
Brain Chamber Six.

08:50.320 --> 08:54.050
[ All shouting ]

08:58.600 --> 09:01.670
Here we are
Chamber number 795.

09:01.710 --> 09:03.680
Bolo's Mind Palace.

09:03.710 --> 09:06.960
Beyond this point,
only one of you may enter,

09:06.990 --> 09:10.100
and it's already
been pre-selected.

09:10.130 --> 09:13.310
Yooooooooou!

09:13.340 --> 09:15.140
You've been chosen.

09:15.170 --> 09:17.860
But then again,
you were already selected

09:17.900 --> 09:20.900
before you were even born!

09:20.930 --> 09:23.140
-We'll be here, Gary.
-You got this!

09:23.180 --> 09:24.420
[ Mooncake cooing ]

09:24.460 --> 09:25.970
[ Grunts ] Hee-hee-hee!

09:26.010 --> 09:27.980
KVN will look after Mooncake,
'cause he's so helpful.

09:28.010 --> 09:30.980
♪ Oh, baby,
KVN's got the magic ♪

09:31.010 --> 09:32.880
♪ And the magic's got KVN

09:32.910 --> 09:33.980
I don't like this.

09:34.020 --> 09:35.570
All this right here,
I don't like.

09:35.600 --> 09:37.050
You're not hanging
out with Mooncake.

09:37.090 --> 09:39.230
You're a bad influence. Okay?
'Cause I don't like you.

09:39.260 --> 09:43.270
♪ Oh, baby, KVN's got the magic,
and the magic's got KVN ♪

09:43.300 --> 09:46.170
♪ KVN's got the magic,
and magic's got KVN ♪

09:46.200 --> 09:47.650
You're the worst.

09:47.690 --> 09:49.510
Good luck, Gary.

09:49.550 --> 09:53.690
[ Whirring ]

09:56.660 --> 09:59.320
♪♪

09:59.350 --> 10:01.600
Bolo: Come forth, Gary.

10:01.630 --> 10:04.630
♪♪

10:04.670 --> 10:06.950
Oh, my gosh. Okay.

10:06.980 --> 10:08.260
Ohh...

10:08.290 --> 10:10.640
Oh -- ah!

10:10.670 --> 10:11.640
Aah!

10:11.680 --> 10:13.190
Okay. This is new.

10:13.230 --> 10:15.260
Bolo: In order
to face what's ahead,

10:15.300 --> 10:19.200
you need to face
what's inside of you.

10:19.230 --> 10:20.300
[ Gasps ]

10:20.340 --> 10:21.550
Oh, look!

10:21.580 --> 10:23.860
There's
a Construction Hat Gary.

10:23.890 --> 10:24.930
Hey!

10:24.960 --> 10:27.210
[ Gasps ]
There's an Eagle-Faced Gary.

10:27.240 --> 10:28.550
[ Screeching ] Hi!

10:28.590 --> 10:30.350
[ Gasps ]
Cookie-Headed Gary.

10:30.380 --> 10:31.760
Hi. What's up?

10:31.800 --> 10:33.520
Oh, my gosh!

10:33.560 --> 10:35.110
Little Micro Gary.

10:35.150 --> 10:36.940
-[ High-pitched ] Hey!
-Who's that?

10:36.980 --> 10:39.560
Bolo: That's
the Amazing Mustache Gary.

10:39.600 --> 10:43.710
Gary, you're never gonna
be able to grow one of these.

10:43.740 --> 10:49.470
A thick, rich,
luscious mustache.

10:49.510 --> 10:51.780
[ Moans ]

10:51.820 --> 10:54.550
[ Moans ] Hell yeah,
that feels good!

10:54.580 --> 10:55.860
It's true.

10:55.890 --> 10:57.410
I've never been able
to grow a mustache.

10:57.440 --> 11:03.040
I wish I was a crumb,
so I could get caught in this.

11:03.070 --> 11:04.380
What are you doing,
Mustache Gary?

11:04.420 --> 11:08.840
Combing my Mustache with
my Little Mustache Comb!

11:08.870 --> 11:12.740
But you'll never know
the satisfaction of that.

11:12.770 --> 11:14.910
[ Laughs ]

11:14.950 --> 11:18.360
Oh, it feels
so gooooood!

11:18.400 --> 11:20.090
Ugh, it's so true.

11:20.120 --> 11:21.750
I won't.

11:21.780 --> 11:23.540
[ Groans ] Oh, no.

11:23.570 --> 11:24.850
What is this?

11:24.890 --> 11:26.090
Aah! What's happening?!

11:26.130 --> 11:28.820
Bolo: Your anxiety
is consuming you.

11:28.860 --> 11:31.620
-[ Groans ]
-You know you can't succeed.

11:31.650 --> 11:33.720
Because I can't
grow a 'stache?

11:33.760 --> 11:37.690
That's exactly why.
[ Laughs ]

11:39.660 --> 11:42.180
Bolo: You're not hero.

11:42.210 --> 11:45.290
Your father was.

11:45.320 --> 11:47.250
[ Gasping ]

11:47.290 --> 11:49.050
You're right.

11:49.080 --> 11:51.290
He would've
figured this out.

11:51.330 --> 11:54.050
I'm scared there's
no winning this,

11:54.090 --> 11:55.780
that there's no way
to close this breach

11:55.810 --> 11:58.750
without losing my friends.

11:58.780 --> 12:00.470
Okay.

12:00.510 --> 12:02.030
Let's not
do that again!

12:02.060 --> 12:05.410
All progress begins
with the truth.

12:05.440 --> 12:07.580
We're running
out of time.

12:07.620 --> 12:10.970
I need to know right now
how to close this breach.

12:11.000 --> 12:14.590
I don't have the answer for you,
but he will.

12:14.630 --> 12:17.590
Who the hell is "He Will?"
I don't know a "He Will."

12:17.630 --> 12:20.560
You'll only have
a short time.

12:20.600 --> 12:24.810
[ Whirring ]

12:29.360 --> 12:31.160
Hello?

12:31.190 --> 12:37.790
♪♪

12:37.820 --> 12:39.170
Dad.

12:41.450 --> 12:42.830
What's going on
with Gary?

12:42.860 --> 12:45.240
-He's fine.
-Show them, Gatekeeper.

12:45.280 --> 12:46.590
Reveal your secrets!

12:46.620 --> 12:49.490
And if you hit me,
I will end you.

12:49.520 --> 12:52.800
Oh, my gosh!
You are all so sassy!

12:52.840 --> 12:56.120
Just watch
and leave me alone already.

12:56.150 --> 12:59.190
Bolo:
Mooncake, follow my voice.

12:59.220 --> 13:01.910
-Chockity.
-KVN, stop touching stuff.

13:01.950 --> 13:04.190
♪ And the magic's got KVN

13:04.230 --> 13:05.190
Everybody!

13:05.230 --> 13:07.470
Dad, it's me, Gary.

13:07.510 --> 13:09.470
Dad?
Who the hell are you?

13:09.510 --> 13:11.340
And why did time freeze?

13:11.370 --> 13:12.790
Did you freeze time?

13:12.820 --> 13:14.440
You time-freezing demon!

13:14.480 --> 13:16.270
Whoa! Okay, look.
I don't think you would

13:16.310 --> 13:18.280
believe me if I told you
how I got here.

13:18.310 --> 13:20.830
But I'm telling you
I am your son.

13:20.860 --> 13:24.660
My son is much younger,
a boy half your age.

13:24.700 --> 13:28.350
If you're really my son,
what was the promise?

13:28.390 --> 13:29.980
What?
Before I left.

13:30.010 --> 13:31.980
To have my adventures.

13:32.010 --> 13:35.530
Bunches and bunches
of them.

13:35.570 --> 13:37.190
Is it really you?

13:37.230 --> 13:39.370
As real as it gets, Dad.

13:42.200 --> 13:45.720
Oh, hell yeah.

13:45.750 --> 13:48.170
♪♪

13:48.200 --> 13:49.890
What the hell
are you doing here?

13:49.930 --> 13:52.210
It's a real novel, but I'm
trying to save the Earth --

13:52.240 --> 13:54.590
actually universe sounds
way cooler,

13:54.620 --> 13:57.000
so I'm actually gonna say
"universe" from now on.

13:57.040 --> 13:58.350
You're what?

13:58.380 --> 14:00.730
I'm trying to find out how
to close a breach in space

14:00.770 --> 14:02.560
that will most certainly
destroy Earth --

14:02.600 --> 14:04.390
actually universe --
in my time.

14:04.420 --> 14:05.740
God, that sounds so cool.

14:05.770 --> 14:08.600
I really feel cool
saying that out loud.

14:08.640 --> 14:09.770
Well, that's what
I'm doing now!

14:09.810 --> 14:11.740
What?You're doing what I'm doing.

14:11.780 --> 14:13.500
I'm doing what you're doing!No way!

14:13.540 --> 14:15.230
Look!

14:15.260 --> 14:17.400
You're closing
the breach in space?

14:17.440 --> 14:19.410
Me and my co-pilot, yeah.

14:19.440 --> 14:26.410
♪♪

14:26.450 --> 14:33.350
♪♪

14:33.380 --> 14:34.420
What is he doing here?!

14:34.450 --> 14:35.800
Jack's my co-pilot.

14:35.840 --> 14:37.700
We've been doing missions
together for years.

14:37.730 --> 14:40.910
Jack?! This guy
is the Lord Commander!

14:40.940 --> 14:43.080
-Who?
-The guy who ripped my arm off

14:43.120 --> 14:45.710
with his mind
and killed my best friend.

14:45.740 --> 14:47.120
Jack is my co-pilot.

14:47.160 --> 14:50.890
He's been my friend
for 29 years.

14:50.920 --> 14:52.750
But I'll take
your word for it.

14:52.780 --> 14:55.610
Well, what do you say we beat
the crap out of him, son?

14:55.650 --> 14:58.200
You are my dad.

14:58.240 --> 14:59.790
Hey!

14:59.820 --> 15:01.240
You sick sack of --

15:01.270 --> 15:02.380
Gah!

15:02.410 --> 15:03.620
Ha! Heyyy!

15:03.660 --> 15:04.930
Heyyyyyy!

15:04.970 --> 15:06.590
Multiple punches
in the face!

15:06.620 --> 15:10.110
Every boy dreams of building
cherished memories...

15:10.150 --> 15:11.840
-Harder!
-...with his dad.

15:11.870 --> 15:14.460
-Like this.
-Kick him in the nuts!

15:14.490 --> 15:15.630
Oh, and this!

15:15.670 --> 15:16.740
Oh, and these!

15:16.770 --> 15:18.640
-[ Laughs ]
-Hyah!

15:18.670 --> 15:21.780
-That's my boy.
-[ Laughs ]

15:21.810 --> 15:23.500
When was the last time
you saw me?

15:23.540 --> 15:26.440
Right before
this mission.

15:26.470 --> 15:27.610
You never came back.

15:27.650 --> 15:28.820
Hm.

15:28.850 --> 15:30.960
So, I'm about to die,
huh?

15:30.990 --> 15:32.480
Not if I can help it.

15:32.510 --> 15:34.760
So how are we gonna
close this breach?

15:34.790 --> 15:36.310
I need to know for me.

15:36.340 --> 15:37.970
An anti-matter bomb
detonated

15:38.000 --> 15:39.970
at the event horizon
of the breach.

15:40.000 --> 15:42.250
The thing is,
right before you came aboard,

15:42.280 --> 15:45.530
an energy blast in Final Space
was about to hit our ship.

15:45.560 --> 15:48.600
Time froze, and now there's
no way to deliver the bomb.

15:48.630 --> 15:50.320
Unless...
Hit me.

15:50.360 --> 15:51.500
[ Thwack! ]
Nice.

15:51.530 --> 15:54.670
Thanks. What if you take out
the bomb manually?

15:54.710 --> 15:56.120
That could work.
Really?

15:56.160 --> 15:59.510
Wow, I mean,
we could do it together.

15:59.540 --> 16:01.820
Bolo: Mooncake.

16:01.850 --> 16:03.270
It's time you knew.

16:03.300 --> 16:05.100
Whoa, look at all
this cool brain stuff.

16:05.130 --> 16:09.340
Hmm. That's mine, and that's
mine, and that's mine.

16:09.380 --> 16:11.900
Hey, let's do Jell-O shots
with the grain goo!

16:13.380 --> 16:17.010
You're the key
to Final Space...

16:17.040 --> 16:19.870
because that's what
you're made of.

16:19.900 --> 16:21.670
Final Space.

16:21.700 --> 16:28.330
♪♪

16:28.360 --> 16:31.090
Chockity.

16:32.680 --> 16:36.020
We'll need to take out the
primary and secondary trigger.

16:36.060 --> 16:38.030
Right. I have no idea
what that is,

16:38.060 --> 16:41.550
so I'm gonna look at you
and nod in agreement.

16:41.580 --> 16:44.550
So, you met anybody?

16:44.580 --> 16:46.030
No, well, kind of.

16:46.070 --> 16:48.210
I'm seeing two people
at the same time -- but mainly,

16:48.240 --> 16:51.250
I'm not like cheating because
they're the same person.

16:51.280 --> 16:53.040
Got it.
Time-travel thing?

16:53.080 --> 16:55.040
Yes!
Been there.

16:55.080 --> 16:57.250
Ha! [ Laughs ]

16:57.290 --> 16:58.600
Nice pair.

16:58.630 --> 17:00.050
What's their name?
Quinn.

17:00.080 --> 17:01.570
What's she like?

17:01.600 --> 17:04.190
The younger hot one?
Or the older equally hot one?

17:04.230 --> 17:05.710
The one in your
timeline.

17:05.740 --> 17:09.750
Well, she's headstrong,
focused, and a real leader.

17:09.780 --> 17:10.960
Do you love her?
Ohh!

17:10.990 --> 17:13.200
[ Laughs nervously ]
To the max-core.

17:13.230 --> 17:17.100
But I don't think she thinks
very much of me.

17:17.130 --> 17:18.790
Really? You're a catch.

17:18.830 --> 17:20.240
You think I'm a catch?
You -- you think so?

17:20.280 --> 17:23.930
I'm looking at you,
I'm seeing a catch.

17:23.970 --> 17:25.520
All right,
it's ready to go.

17:25.560 --> 17:28.350
You sure there isn't anything
else that needs to be done?

17:28.390 --> 17:30.730
Bomb-wise?
Anything else at all?

17:30.770 --> 17:32.120
That's it. Let's go.

17:32.150 --> 17:33.700
We could get lunch.

17:33.740 --> 17:36.120
You want to get lunch?

17:39.120 --> 17:40.090
Son.

17:40.120 --> 17:42.640
Grab the plasma torch.

17:42.680 --> 17:46.090
♪♪

17:46.130 --> 17:48.300
What are you doing?
Dad!

17:48.340 --> 17:50.100
Dad, don't do this
without me!

17:50.130 --> 17:52.100
[ Grunts ]Son, you have your own time

17:52.140 --> 17:53.550
to worry about.

17:53.580 --> 17:55.410
[ Grunting ]

17:55.450 --> 17:57.110
Dad! This --

17:57.140 --> 17:58.280
This was my idea.

17:58.310 --> 18:00.280
Yeah, but it's
my responsibility.

18:00.320 --> 18:02.800
There's another
anti-matter bomb in New York.

18:02.840 --> 18:04.110
The one on Earth.

18:04.150 --> 18:07.080
Use it to close
this breach in your time.

18:07.120 --> 18:10.290
You know, I had only
one regret when I left.

18:10.330 --> 18:12.090
Thought I was never
gonna get the chance

18:12.120 --> 18:14.330
to see the man
you would've grown up to be.

18:14.360 --> 18:19.300
Well, now I know he's better
than I would've ever hoped.

18:19.330 --> 18:20.990
Please don't.
Stop. Please.

18:21.030 --> 18:23.820
Stop. Stop. Stop! Stop!

18:23.860 --> 18:25.650
No! Please no!

18:25.690 --> 18:27.520
Stop!

18:27.550 --> 18:29.410
[ Beeps ]

18:29.450 --> 18:31.170
♪♪

18:31.210 --> 18:32.660
I'm not gonna let you die.

18:32.690 --> 18:34.110
Not again.

18:34.140 --> 18:35.830
I'm gonna come get you!

18:35.870 --> 18:37.870
Make me a promise,
son.

18:37.900 --> 18:39.600
Save the Earth.

18:39.630 --> 18:41.150
Nah, you're right.

18:41.180 --> 18:43.150
"Universe"
sounds much cooler.

18:43.190 --> 18:45.530
What if I can't do it?

18:45.570 --> 18:47.160
Try your best.

18:47.190 --> 18:49.950
What if my best
isn't good enough?

18:49.990 --> 18:52.020
It's good enough
for me.

18:52.060 --> 19:03.480
♪♪

19:03.520 --> 19:14.730
♪♪

19:14.770 --> 19:17.700
Noooooooooo!

19:17.740 --> 19:19.670
No.

19:19.710 --> 19:21.850
♪♪

19:21.880 --> 19:23.020
Aaah!

19:23.050 --> 19:25.330
Oh, God!

19:25.370 --> 19:28.680
Aaaah!

19:28.710 --> 19:30.750
[ Snarls ]

19:30.790 --> 19:38.690
♪♪

19:47.560 --> 19:53.530
♪♪

19:53.570 --> 19:56.600
[ Sobbing ]

19:56.640 --> 19:58.570
Why?

20:00.750 --> 20:04.130
Didn't know we were members
of the same club.

20:04.160 --> 20:07.100
Gary, you still
want to do this?

20:09.760 --> 20:11.340
I'll try my best.

20:11.380 --> 20:13.070
That's good enough
for me.

20:13.100 --> 20:15.110
Wait -- were you watching
me and my dad?

20:15.140 --> 20:16.380
No.

20:16.420 --> 20:17.520
No.

20:17.560 --> 20:22.910
♪♪

20:22.940 --> 20:24.740
Where are you going?

20:24.770 --> 20:27.430
They don't need
me anymore.

20:27.460 --> 20:39.580
♪♪

20:39.610 --> 20:41.060
Should we get up?

20:41.100 --> 20:43.310
No. We have
a little time.

20:43.340 --> 20:45.070
Actually, you don't!

20:45.100 --> 20:47.450
Get off
your sass buckets!!

20:47.480 --> 20:50.420
♪♪

20:50.450 --> 20:53.630
H.U.E.: Gary, is Nightfall
not coming with us?

20:53.660 --> 20:55.010
No.

20:55.040 --> 20:56.490
You think you know a person,

20:56.530 --> 20:58.910
and then something
like this happens.

20:58.940 --> 21:00.430
What course
should I set?

21:00.460 --> 21:01.320
Earth.

21:01.360 --> 21:03.120
Or actually,
no, the Universe.

21:03.150 --> 21:04.470
We're gonna save the --
Well actually,

21:04.500 --> 21:05.950
well, that's doesn't even
make any dang sense.

21:05.980 --> 21:07.780
Okay, just Earth.
Earth...

21:07.810 --> 21:08.780
Earth.

21:08.810 --> 21:10.780
We've got a bomb to find.

21:10.820 --> 21:17.440
♪♪
